@abstract:
Declared intent, purpose, and scope for Bundle of Joy (BoJ) Server.
LLM/SLM agents: understand what this repo IS and IS NOT before acting.
@end

@requires:
- section: Purpose
- section: Anti-Purpose
- section: Architectural-Invariants
@end

## Purpose

BoJ (Bundle of Joy) is a unified MCP server that consolidates all hyperpolymath
tooling into a single endpoint. It provides Claude Code integration for GitHub,
GitLab, Cloudflare, Vercel, Verpex, Gmail, Calendar, browser automation, research,
ML, and 125 open-source cartridges. It implements a three-class architecture:
- Class 1 (Simple Track): zero-infrastructure CLI/curl workflows
- Class 2 (Orchestrator Track): HMAC-SHA256 webhooks and real-time MQTT/WS
- Class 3 (Multiplier Track): Elixir/BEAM mass concurrency

## Anti-Purpose

BoJ is NOT:
- A general-purpose API gateway or reverse proxy
- A standalone application — it serves LLM/MCP tool consumers
- A replacement for direct API access when MCP is not involved
- A container for business logic for connected services (GitHub, GitLab, etc.)
- A standalone MCP server outside the BoJ architecture (all MCP goes through BoJ)

## Architectural-Invariants

These must not be reversed without an explicit ADR:
- Three-class architecture: Class 1 must never be broken by Class 2/3 features
- MCP bridge is the sole entry point for Claude Code integration
- REST API on port 7700 for all cartridge invocations
- Self-contained cartridges with own adapters in cartridges/<name>/adapter/
- All MCP through BoJ only — no standalone MCP servers permitted
- Firefox first for browser automation (not Chrome)
- HMAC-SHA256 webhook verification for Class 2 orchestrator track
- Target runtime: Zig→WASM typed bridge (Node.js mcp-bridge is transitional)

## Sensitive-Areas

Ask before touching:
- mcp-bridge/ — MCP protocol bridge; changes affect all Claude Code integration
- adapter/ — service adapters (GitHub, GitLab, Cloudflare, etc.); API contract changes
- cartridges/ — self-contained service cartridges; each has own adapter
- ffi/ — Idris2 ABI + Zig FFI interface layer
- .machine_readable/ — checkpoint files, format is specified
- ai-plugin.json — cartridge metadata; must remain valid for discovery

## Ecosystem

- belongs-to: standalone server (not a library)
- depends-on: github-api, gitlab-api, cloudflare-api, vercel-api, verpex-api
- depended-on-by: claude-code, panll, hypatia, ambientops
